  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records strongly establish that Monte Carlo or hybrid MC/MD methods can generate and tune chemical short-range order in bcc refractory high-entropy alloys, and they show that such order can form favored elemental associations, precipitates, or ordered structures. Separately, R6 identifies lattice distortion and defects as causes of suppressed phonon and electron propagation in the exact HfNbTaTiZr system, while R16 provides related evidence for an ordered B2 mediator in a refractory alloy. An expert could therefore plausibly propose applying MC-induced SRO to HfNbTaTiZr and testing whether ordering reduces lattice distortion and raises thermal conductivity. However, none of the records connects SRO to thermal transport, predicts HfTi/TiZr clusters or percolating high-conductivity pathways, or describes the corresponding high-frequency phonon-density-of-states changes. Those central mechanistic links require a substantial additional idea, so the set points in the right direction without fully reconstructing the later result."
